message:
{{#is_alert}}
Mongo-backed detector observed 10 fresh Node 2 soil-humidity readings with range <= 0.01 over the recent window. This indicates the greenhouse_a telemetry stream is flatlined; it does not prove a physical probe failure. Inspect sample freshness, MQTT bridge, and Mongo persistence before action. The attached workflow can only place the virtual output in SAFE HOLD; it cannot command physical pumps or PLCs.
[Open correlated Node 2 logs](https://app.datadoghq.com/logs?query=service%3Asmiot-smart-farm%20%40farm.key%3Agreenhouse_a%20%40node.id%3A2%20%40source%3Asmiot_demo_stream)
@workflow-smiot-node-2-safe-mode-hold-and-verify
{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_recovery}}
The Mongo-backed flatline signal returned to 0. The application recovery verifier checks monitor state, fresh varying Node 2 MongoDB samples, the acknowledged HOLD record, and virtual PLC acknowledgement. It sends CLEAR only when every check passes; simulated pump outputs must remain OFF. This proves telemetry recovery, not physical sensor repair.
[Open correlated Node 2 logs](https://app.datadoghq.com/logs?query=service%3Asmiot-smart-farm%20%40farm.key%3Agreenhouse_a%20%40node.id%3A2%20%40source%3Asmiot_demo_stream)
{{/is_recovery}}
